	"department": "HIST",
	"description": [
		"This seminar explores the development of the discipline of history, from its beginnings in the Ancient world to the present. Students investigate methodological and stylistic innovations in the Medieval and Early Modern periods that later formed the basis for history's emergence as an academic discipline in the nineteenth century. It features intellectual trends that have transformed historical research and writing over the last one-hundred years, resulting in a number of important \"turns\" influenced by other disciplines, ranging from sociology and anthropology to linguistics. In addition to reading some of the most influential texts in the discipline, students conduct research on a historiographical topic of their choosing."
	],
